<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19793" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grădārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to steps</i>, <i>going</i> or <i>proceeding step by
				step</i> (very rare; not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: equus gradarius, <i>a
				pacer</i>, <i>ambler</i>, Lucil. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 17, 25</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pugna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 473</span></i>
			 P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of a deliberate speaker: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cicero quoque noster gradarius fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 40, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
